00:51:13.060 --> 00:51:18.060
So anyway, there's like 36 people there too

00:51:18.060 --> 00:51:22.060
who are still there and a Guantanamo

00:51:22.060 --> 00:51:27.060
who will probably be there if the Pentagon has its way.

00:51:27.060 --> 00:51:29.060
They will be there forever.

00:51:29.060 --> 00:51:32.060
And out of these 36 men,

00:51:32.060 --> 00:51:37.060
they did nothing that we know of before they were arrested,

00:51:37.060 --> 00:51:39.060
before they got to Guantanamo.

00:51:39.060 --> 00:51:41.060
They were never a threat to the United States.

00:51:41.060 --> 00:51:43.060
They would never hurt any of us.

00:51:43.060 --> 00:51:48.060
But now, for 12 years, they've been in solitary confinement,

00:51:48.060 --> 00:51:51.060
they've been force fed, they've been tortured.

00:51:51.060 --> 00:51:56.760
They can't let them go because they might hurt us.

00:51:56.760 --> 00:52:00.760
And this is not my take on it.

00:52:00.760 --> 00:52:05.760
This is what the Pentagon says about why these people cannot be released.

00:52:05.760 --> 00:52:08.760
So these are the people,

00:52:08.760 --> 00:52:14.760
the people who made the decision about who would go to Guantanamo

00:52:14.760 --> 00:52:16.760
are the exact same people.

00:52:16.760 --> 00:52:19.760
And if you look up this article in the Times, it names them.

00:52:19.760 --> 00:52:22.760
These are the exact same people who are now targeting,

00:52:22.760 --> 00:52:24.760
deciding who's going to die.

00:52:24.760 --> 00:52:27.760
So when you hear that a bad guy got killed,

00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:31.760
in Al-Qaeda, this Fruq Akhmet Farrouk,

00:52:31.760 --> 00:52:35.760
that he was a bad guy, that he was an accomplice with Al-Qaeda,

00:52:35.760 --> 00:52:38.760
take it with a grain of salt because we don't know

00:52:38.760 --> 00:52:42.760
and there was no indictment, there was no charge.

00:52:42.760 --> 00:52:45.760
This is just assassination.

00:52:45.760 --> 00:52:48.760
These are simply murder victims, all of them.

00:52:48.760 --> 00:52:51.760
These strikes, no matter what it is they did,

00:52:51.760 --> 00:52:54.760
as Patrick could tell you as a lawyer,

00:52:54.760 --> 00:52:58.760
it's against the law to kill a gangster on the street.

00:52:58.760 --> 00:53:02.760
No matter how bad somebody is, they should have a trial

00:53:02.760 --> 00:53:05.760
and you just can't kill them because you feel like it,

00:53:05.760 --> 00:53:09.760
because you think they're bad or they look like somebody who's bad.

00:53:09.760 --> 00:53:12.760
This strike, they killed these two American citizens

00:53:12.760 --> 00:53:14.760
and this Italian man and how many others,

00:53:14.760 --> 00:53:16.760
what they call a signature strike,

00:53:16.760 --> 00:53:19.760
they're simply looking at the patterns of behavior

00:53:19.760 --> 00:53:22.760
and deciding that because people were acting a certain way

00:53:22.760 --> 00:53:26.760
around this building there must be something nefarious going on in there.

00:53:26.760 --> 00:53:28.760
So the strike happened.

00:53:28.760 --> 00:53:33.760
It's exactly as reflected in our cities with racial profiling.

